  - monitoring
  - llm
  - information-flow
abstract: >-
  A monitor that reads one agent at a time misses a harmful objective split
  across several agents, and in a fleet of hundreds of agents a defender
  doesn't know which agents to read together. This repository follows the
  data instead: a cheap decision model labels every action, a graph traces
  where private data can travel across agents, and an LLM monitor reads only
  the groups the graph finds. It compares that with a tool-using monitor over
  the raw log and with a provenance graph, in fleets of up to 4,803 agents.
  Written for Apart Research's Swarm Alignment Hackathon (Track 4: Multi-Agent
  Oversight and Control), 6 to 8 November 2026.
